  "kind": "statement",
  "title": "The $L^2$-weight is at most the weight",
  "statement": "Let $\\mathcal F$ be a lisse Weil sheaf of rank $r$ on the affine\ncurve $X_0$, punctually $\\iota$-mixed of weights at most $w$.\nThen\n\n$$\n\\|\\mathcal F\\|\\le w.\n$$",
  "source": {
    "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-deligne-laumon-a1/sk-l-dl-a1-energy/lem-wf-l2-upper.md",
    "place": "node lem-wf-l2-upper, order 2760"
  },
  "stmt_deps": [],
  "proof": [
    {
      "text": "At $y\\in X_0(k_m)$ the eigenvalues of the Frobenius $F_y^{(m)}$\nare the $m/d(y)$-th powers of the local eigenvalues at the closed\npoint below, hence have modulus at most $q^{mw/2}$ by the punctual\nbounds of [def-weil-punctual-weights]; therefore\n\n$$\n\\|f_{\\mathcal F}\\|_m^2\\le r^2\\cdot\\#X_0(k_m)\\cdot q^{mw}\n\\le C\\,q^{m(w+1)}\n$$\n\nfor a constant $C$ (the point-count bound of the affine curve,\n[lem-wf-point-count-linear-growth] of the basic-weight chapter). The\n$\\limsup$ in [def-wf-l2-norm] is therefore $0$ for\n$\\beta>w$, hence $\\|\\mathcal F\\|\\le w$.",
      "uses": [
        "def-weil-punctual-weights",
        "lem-wf-point-count-linear-growth",
        "def-wf-l2-norm"
      ],
      "elementary": false
    }
  ],
